## Approach

Two new pieces in the review pipeline: (1) on-demand biomarkers (`function_hotspot`, `code_age_volatility`) computed via git blame at review time — too expensive for the parse-time pipeline, and (2) a health delta section comparing current per-file health scores (stored findings + on-demand findings) against the latest snapshot. Both share a `BlameCache` to avoid redundant git calls within a single review run.

Alternative considered: persisting blame in the DB for cross-run caching. Rejected — blame is only needed at review time, an in-memory cache within a single invocation is sufficient, and avoids a new migration. "Commit-based invalidation" is natural: each review invocation is at a fixed HEAD, dedupe is by file path within that run.

The `FunctionHotspot` and `CodeAgeVolatility` variants already exist in the `BiomarkerKind` enum with weights and categories assigned — no schema or enum changes needed.

